    "Casey's answer (PR #66 comment 6968763406, item 2), as PR #67 words it in lnk_04: \"A receipt belongs to the link-hour of the clock hour that holds its `received_at`, half-open: a receipt exactly on the hour belongs to the later hour only\". The link-hour's grain is (relayer, gateway, hour) (lnk_08).",
    "c47-r's receipts at c47-g are direct hops at 10:40, 10:50, 11:00:00, 11:10 and 11:20 (lnk_01). Both ends are stationary, on c20 and g16, and every receipt passes lnk_05 at 2745.603 m: all five are counted.",
    "The 11:00:00 receipt belongs to the 11:00 hour, which counts it with 11:10 and 11:20: 3 packets, kept. The 10:00 hour counts 10:40 and 10:50: 2 packets, dropped by lnk_04. Placed in the 10:00 hour, the 11:00:00 receipt would make that hour 3 packets and this one 2.",
    "Medians in the 11:00 hour: SNR 5, 6 and 7 dB give 6.0; RSSI -90, -95 and -100 dBm give -95.0. position_uncertainty_m is c20 22.734410 m plus g16 363.750397 m, = 386.484807 m. Neither end is precise."
